-- title:
--   Honda system of an isogeny kernel as a cokernel
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbf Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel $(p)$, and complete for the $(p)$-adic topology. Let $\Lambda,\Lambda'$ be commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebras, finite and free over $\mathcal O$ of rank a power of $p$, such that the Cartier duals $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbf Z/p}(\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\Lambda,\mathbf Z/p)$ and likewise for $\Lambda'$ are local rings. Let $r,v\in\mathbf N$ and let $H_1=(F,V,L)$ be a Honda system for the element $p$ on $\mathcal O^r$: $\mathcal O$-linear $F,V$ with $F\circ V=V\circ F=p\cdot\mathrm{id}$, and a submodule $L$ with every element of $L\cap\operatorname{range}F$ of the form $p\,y$ with $y\in L$, with $p\,y\in\operatorname{range}F$ for $y\in L$, with $\operatorname{range}F+L=\mathcal O^r$, and with $V$ injective on $L$. Let $\pi\colon\mathcal O^r\to M(\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\Lambda)$ be an additive surjection onto the Dieudonné module (the direct limit over $n$ of the groups of primitive truncated Witt vectors of length $n$) whose kernel is exactly $p^v\mathcal O^r$, which carries $F$ to Frobenius and $V$ to Verschiebung, and for which the Fontaine–Hodge subgroup attached to the inclusion $\Lambda\to\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\Lambda$ is the image $\pi(L)$; let $\pi'\colon\mathcal O^r\to M(\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\Lambda')$ be an additive surjection. Let $f\colon\Lambda'\to\Lambda$ be a bialgebra map over $\mathcal O$ and $\varphi$ an $\mathcal O$-linear endomorphism of $\mathcal O^r$ with $p^v\mathcal O^r\subseteq\operatorname{range}\varphi$ and $M(\mathbf Z/p\otimes f)\circ\pi'=\pi\circ\varphi$. Finally let $H$ be a commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra, finite and free over $\mathcal O$, and $q\colon\Lambda\to H$ a surjective bialgebra map whose kernel as an ideal equals the ideal generated by $f(\ker\varepsilon_{\Lambda'})$. Then $\rho:=M(\mathbf Z/p\otimes q)\circ\pi$ is surjective, its kernel is exactly $\operatorname{range}\varphi$, it carries $F$ to Frobenius and $V$ to Verschiebung, and the Fontaine–Hodge subgroup attached to the inclusion $H\to\mathbf Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}H$ equals $\rho(L)$. No $p$-power rank or local-Cartier-dual hypothesis is imposed on $H$.
--
--   This is the step in Fontaine's classification of finite flat commutative $p$-groups over $W(k)$ by finite Honda systems which computes the Honda system of the kernel of a homomorphism of unipotent groups as the cokernel of the associated map of free Honda systems. It is used in the construction of a $p$-divisible tower realising a prescribed Dieudonné-module datum over $\mathbf Z_p$.
